OL,3,GNEWSAFallen WW2 soldier's body
OL,4,Aidentified 81 years on
OL,5,
OL,6,FA fallen World War Two soldier has been
OL,7,Fcommemorated after his body was
OL,8,Fidentified 81 years after his death.
OL,10,FL/Cpl Ronald Smirthwaite, who was born
OL,11,Fin Sheffield, was killed in the
OL,12,FNetherlands in 1945 while fighting with
OL,13,Fthe Hallamshire Batallion and buried in
OL,14,Fan unmarked grave.
OL,16,FThe Ministry of Defence (MoD) said
OL,17,FSmirthwaite's identity had been
OL,18,Fconfirmed after "extensive research"
OL,19,Fand the grave, in Jonkerbos War
OL,20,FCemetery, in the Dutch city of
OL,21,FNijmegen, had been marked with his name
OL,22,Fat a special service.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,389,380,200,160,0,100
